HALTED 2026-09-16.

The presence of this file stops l5-r1-probe: shutdown_requested() returns True,
run_campaign enters safe_shutdown before armed() is consulted, and the process
cancels our outstanding orders, verifies against a fresh venue read, preserves
held inventory to settlement, and idles.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN A RAILWAY VARIABLE. The probe had to be halted
on 2026-09-16 and the only lever that worked was a Railway startCommand
exporting PMUS_SPRING_SHUTDOWN -- the same class of runtime override that
condemned the legacy probe -- because set-variables was unavailable to the
session and redeploy had no snapshot to copy. A halt that depends on a platform
API being reachable is not a halt. This one is a commit.

REMOVING IT DOES NOT AUTHORIZE TRADING. It only un-halts the process. Orders
additionally require a valid, unexpired mandate in analysis/l5/live_mandate.json
naming this service. Both are deliberate: stopping is one decision, authorizing
spend is another, and they should not share a switch.

Reason for this halt: the R1 canary was authorized for ONE market at $0.05,
market #1 settled at 2026-09-16T07:44:32Z, the campaign chain continued on
approvals dated 2026-09-06, and 11+ markets traded with $19.3295 committed to
one of them. See analysis/l5/live_probe/R1_CANARY_BREACH_2026-09-16.md.
